WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.400
I was working at Riverbend Nursing and Rehab Center.

2
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.720
I actually evacuated with my nursing home.

3
00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:17.080
So we took eighty-five geriatrics to Kentwood and housed them in a gymnasium.

4
00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:20.200
We had evacuated before, so it wasn't new to us.

5
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.920
We took all of our residents' mattresses with us.

6
00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:27.200
And we took enough clothing for three days for each resident.

7
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:35.120
And of course we took just huge quantities of things like diapers and medical supplies.

8
00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:41.080
We took all of our medicine carts and just put them in the back of vehicles.

9
00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:50.020
Then we loaded three buses of our residents, and that was tough because most of them couldn't get on the bus.

10
00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:52.600
The employees didn't really stay in the gymnasium.

11
00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:57.920
Some of our CNAs [Certified Nursing Assistants] stayed in an upstairs area with their children.

12
00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:05.360
But it was very tight quarters up there, and we didn't want to impede on the residents, because they didn't have a whole lot of space.

13
00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.480
So most of us slept in our automobiles at night, and then we'd get up.

14
00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:11.320
But we were very fortunate.

15
00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:18.540
We had a couple of guys who had evacuated with us, the maintenance man and his brother.

16
00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:28.860
And they managed to make a makeshift shower, so we were able to keep the residents clean.

17
00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:31.160
We really met all of their needs.

18
00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:38.520
And we laughed, some crew from Red Cross came through, and they, I guess, panicked, seeing that we had all these elderly.

19
00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:42.480
And the first thing they said was that they would be more than happy to bring us food.

20
00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:46.620
Well, we were providing not only three meals a day, but three hot meals a day.

21
00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:51.660
They were getting balanced meals that were hot.

22
00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:56.580
So we just kind of got a kick out of that, because we were managing.

23
00:01:56.580 --> 00:01:58.620
We kind of started to panic.

24
00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:01.760
I'm trying to think, it must have been like Thursday of the first week.

25
00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:05.320
We had all these contracts with people, but nobody could get through.

26
00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:10.180
And I'll never forget, out of nowhere, these three trucks showed up.

27
00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:16.540
It was people from some northern state, I don't even know where they were from, who just decided to get on the road.

28
00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:23.200
And they packaged ice, and just all the basics that they really needed.

29
00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:23.720
Ice!

30
00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:25.640
I never thought ice would be such a thrill.

31
00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:26.760
But we were so happy to get ice.

32
00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:34.320
And they had propane, because we needed propane to run the things for the kitchen, you know.

33
00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.180
And they showed up with all of that.

34
00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:39.760
Don't ever think that one person can't make a difference in this world.
